<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "176"
  info        : "Verifique se UsePAM está habilitado no sshd (usepam yes). Se sshd não existir, considerar N/A como PASS."
  solution    : "No /etc/ssh/sshd_config, garantir: UsePAM yes"
  reference   : "HITSS (SSH) - UsePAM"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( ( ! command -v sshd >/dev/null 2>&1 ) && echo \'PASS\' ) || ( sshd -T 2>/dev/null | grep -iqE '^\\s*usepam\\s+yes\\s*$' && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "177"
  info        : "Verifique se o sudo está instalado"
  solution    : "Instalar pacote sudo"
  reference   : "HITSS (Privilégios) - sudo"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( command -v sudo >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "178"
  info        : "Verifique se o sudo está configurado para usar pty (Defaults ... use_pty)"
  solution    : "Adicionar 'Defaults use_pty' em /etc/sudoers ou /etc/sudoers.d/*"
  reference   : "HITSS (sudo) - use_pty"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( command -v sudo >/dev/null 2>&1 && egrep -iq '^[[:space:]]*Defaults[[:space:]]+.*\\buse_pty\\b' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/* 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "179"
  info        : "Verifique se existe log de comandos sudo (Defaults ... logfile=...)"
  solution    : "Configurar 'Defaults logfile=/var/log/sudo.log' (ou caminho corporativo) em /etc/sudoers(/d)"
  reference   : "HITSS (sudo) - logfile"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( command -v sudo >/dev/null 2>&1 && egrep -iq '^[[:space:]]*Defaults[[:space:]]+.*\\blogfile=' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/* 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "180"
  info        : "Verifique se sudo exige senha (FAIL se existir Defaults ... !authenticate)"
  solution    : "Remover '!authenticate' de Defaults; exigir autenticação"
  reference   : "HITSS (sudo) - authenticate"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -iq '^[[:space:]]*Defaults[[:space:]]+.*!authenticate' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/* 2>/dev/null && echo \'FAIL\') || echo \'PASS\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "181"
  info        : "Verifique se a re-autenticação do sudo não está desabilitada globalmente (FAIL se Defaults ... timestamp_timeout=-1)"
  solution    : "Remover 'timestamp_timeout=-1' de Defaults; definir valor adequado (ex.: 5)"
  reference   : "HITSS (sudo) - timestamp_timeout"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -iq '^[[:space:]]*Defaults[[:space:]]+.*timestamp_timeout=-?1\\b' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/* 2>/dev/null && echo \'FAIL\') || echo \'PASS\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "182"
  info        : "Verifique se o timeout de autenticação do sudo está configurado (Defaults ... timestamp_timeout=...)"
  solution    : "Adicionar 'Defaults timestamp_timeout=<minutos>' em /etc/sudoers(/d)"
  reference   : "HITSS (sudo) - timestamp_timeout"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -iq '^[[:space:]]*Defaults[[:space:]]+.*\\btimestamp_timeout=' /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/* 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "183"
  info        : "Verifique se o acesso ao comando su está restrito (pam_wheel com group=sudo em /etc/pam.d/su)"
  solution    : "Habilitar pam_wheel em /etc/pam.d/su com 'group=sudo' (ou grupo corporativo)"
  reference   : "HITSS (PAM) - su restrito"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*auth[[:space:]]+required[[:space:]]+pam_wheel\\.so.*group=sudo' /etc/pam.d/su 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "186"
  info        : "Verifique se libpam-pwquality está instalado"
  solution    : "Instalar pacote libpam-pwquality"
  reference   : "HITSS (PAM) - pwquality"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( dpkg-query -s libpam-pwquality 2>/dev/null | grep -Eq '^Status: install ok installed' && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "187"
  info        : "Verifique se pam_unix está habilitado (presença de pam_unix.so nos stacks PAM)"
  solution    : "Garantir linhas pam_unix.so nos arquivos PAM relevantes"
  reference   : "HITSS (PAM) - pam_unix"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -Rq 'pam_unix\\.so' /etc/pam.d 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "188"
  info        : "Verifique se pam_faillock está habilitado (presença de pam_faillock.so)"
  solution    : "Configurar pam_faillock em common-auth (preauth/authfail) e common-account"
  reference   : "HITSS (PAM) - \'FAIL\' lock"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -Rq 'pam_faillock\\.so' /etc/pam.d 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "189"
  info        : "Verifique se pam_pwquality está habilitado (presença de pam_pwquality.so)"
  solution    : "Configurar pam_pwquality em common-password"
  reference   : "HITSS (PAM) - pwquality"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -Rq 'pam_pwquality\\.so' /etc/pam.d 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "190"
  info        : "Verifique se pam_pwhistory está habilitado (presença de pam_pwhistory.so)"
  solution    : "Configurar pam_pwhistory em common-password"
  reference   : "BASELINE HITSS"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -Rq 'pam_pwhistory\\.so' /etc/pam.d 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "191"
  info        : "Verifique se password \'FAIL\' ed attempts lockout está configurado (deny)"
  solution    : "Configurar 'deny=<n>' em /etc/security/faillock.conf ou .d/*.conf"
  reference   : "BASELINE HITSS"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -q 'deny\\s*=' /etc/security/faillock.conf /etc/security/faillock.conf.d/*.conf 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "192"
  info        : "Verifique se unlock_time está configurado"
  solution    : "Configurar 'unlock_time=<segundos>' em /etc/security/faillock.conf ou .d/*.conf"
  reference   : "BASELINE HITSS"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -q 'unlock_time\\s*=' /etc/security/faillock.conf /etc/security/faillock.conf.d/*.conf 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "193"
  info        : "Verifique se even_deny_root ou root_unlock_time está configurado"
  solution    : "Configurar 'even_deny_root' e/ou 'root_unlock_time=<segundos>' em \'FAIL\' lock"
  reference   : "BASELINE HITSS"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -q '(^|\\b)even_deny_root(\\b|\\s)' /etc/security/faillock.conf /etc/security/faillock.conf.d/*.conf 2>/dev/null || egrep -q 'root_unlock_time\\s*=' /etc/security/faillock.conf /etc/security/faillock.conf.d/*.conf 2>/dev/null ) && echo \'PASS\' || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "194"
  info        : "Verifique se difok está configurado"
  solution    : "Configurar 'difok=<n>' em /etc/security/pwquality.conf ou .d/*.conf"
  reference   : "BASELINE HITSS"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -q 'difok\\s*=' /etc/security/pwquality.conf /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/*.conf 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "195"
  info        : "Verifique se minlen está configurado"
  solution    : "Configurar 'minlen=<n>' em /etc/security/pwquality.conf ou .d/*.conf"
  reference   : "BASELINE HITSS"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -q 'minlen\\s*=' /etc/security/pwquality.conf /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/*.conf 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "196"
  info        : "Verifique se password complexity está configurada (ucredit/lcredit/dcredit/ocredit ou minclass)"
  solution    : "Configurar créditos de classes (ucredit, lcredit, dcredit, ocredit) e/ou 'minclass=<n>' em pwquality"
  reference   : "BASELINE HITSS"
  see_also    : "CONSULTAR BASELINE HITSS"
  cmd         : "( egrep -Eiq '(^|[[:space:]])(ucredit|lcredit|dcredit|ocredit|minclass)[[:space:]]*=' /etc/security/pwquality.conf /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/*.conf 2>/dev/null && echo \'PASS\' ) || echo \'FAIL\' "
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*pass\\s*$"
</custom_item>

